1
00:00:40,102 --> 00:00:45,733
Man, I thought you're off-duty in five?
They still called you in? Tough luck.

2
00:00:46,317 --> 00:00:50,279
Cap said I could leave my gun and badge
if I'd rather go home

3
00:00:50,362 --> 00:00:55,117
and listen to mama go on and on
about online shopping or whatever.

4
00:00:55,201 --> 00:00:58,037
That's what you get
for choosing the life of a cop.

5
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,955
It just had to fucking rain…

6
00:01:01,123 --> 00:01:03,125
What's your problem? Back it up.

7
00:01:03,209 --> 00:01:04,502
Wanna get shot…

8
00:01:31,779 --> 00:01:33,197
Got a cyberpsycho!

9
00:01:33,864 --> 00:01:35,950
Raise MaxTac now!

10
00:02:31,255 --> 00:02:33,007
Fry his system.

11
00:02:33,090 --> 00:02:34,967
Freak's got military-grade ICE!

12
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:36,886
So is ours.

13
00:02:36,969 --> 00:02:37,845
Go!

14
00:03:29,313 --> 00:03:30,773
So wacked!

15
00:03:59,677 --> 00:04:01,804
What?! Cut it out, man!

16
00:04:15,567 --> 00:04:18,404
Cycle suspended due to insufficient funds…

17
00:04:18,487 --> 00:04:21,031
Not again…

18
00:04:21,573 --> 00:04:25,577
Tragedy in Westbrook. A corporate convoy
was ambushed by 6th Street…

19
00:04:25,661 --> 00:04:27,871
Jeez, mom…

20
00:04:30,249 --> 00:04:31,250
Morning.

21
00:04:31,333 --> 00:04:35,004
Sleeping on the couch again?
You know you've got a bed.

22
00:04:35,087 --> 00:04:37,881
Just dead after my night shift is all.

23
00:04:37,965 --> 00:04:40,342
You and the washing machine both.

24
00:04:40,426 --> 00:04:41,635
Forget to re-up it?

25
00:04:41,719 --> 00:04:42,886
Yeah…

26
00:04:42,970 --> 00:04:44,638
I'll do it later, 'kay?

27
00:04:44,722 --> 00:04:50,311
Speaking of money, when did you say
you needed that update for class?

28
00:04:50,394 --> 00:04:54,565
It's fine. Got Doc to handle it.

29
00:04:54,648 --> 00:04:56,734
"Handle it"?

30
00:04:56,817 --> 00:04:58,152
Yep, all set.

31
00:04:58,235 --> 00:05:00,571
Don't go cutting corners, Dee.

32
00:05:00,654 --> 00:05:04,408
I'm getting paid tonight,
so you get it properly updated, okay?

33
00:05:04,491 --> 00:05:07,745
It's fine. We don't even have enough
to re-up the washing machine.

34
00:05:07,828 --> 00:05:09,788
I told you I just forgot.

35
00:05:09,872 --> 00:05:12,624
Promise me you'll buy the update.

36
00:05:12,708 --> 00:05:14,418
Okay, okay.

37
00:05:14,501 --> 00:05:17,087
Are you going to school dressed like that?

38
00:05:17,171 --> 00:05:18,881
My uniform's soaked.

39
00:05:18,964 --> 00:05:21,425
A military-grade implant
was found missing from

40
00:05:21,508 --> 00:05:24,386
the body of Lt. Col. James Norris
who was shot dead by MaxTac…

41
00:05:24,470 --> 00:05:26,722
Mom, you're on TV!

42
00:05:26,805 --> 00:05:27,806
Nova!

43
00:05:27,890 --> 00:05:30,184
Not nova, David. A bloodbath.

44
00:05:30,768 --> 00:05:32,353
Go on, off to school.

45
00:05:32,436 --> 00:05:33,687
Fine.

46
00:05:34,438 --> 00:05:36,065
Love you.

47
00:05:40,694 --> 00:05:41,695
Maine?

48
00:05:41,779 --> 00:05:42,988
It's Gloria.

49
00:06:31,036 --> 00:06:35,332
Trauma Team. Clear the way immediately.

50
00:06:35,415 --> 00:06:38,001
Emergency evac underway.

51
00:06:38,085 --> 00:06:40,587
All AVs immediately vacate the airway.

52
00:06:40,671 --> 00:06:42,297
I repeat. Trauma Team…

53
00:08:01,376 --> 00:08:02,753
Good morning, class.

54
00:08:02,836 --> 00:08:05,797
Today's attendance, zero absences.

55
00:08:05,881 --> 00:08:07,799
Martinez, David.

56
00:08:07,883 --> 00:08:10,302
You are not wearing the Academy uniform.

57
00:08:10,385 --> 00:08:14,306
Sorry. It's still at the cleaner's.

58
00:08:14,389 --> 00:08:16,141
Where is your spare?

59
00:08:16,225 --> 00:08:18,101
The spare's there too.

60
00:08:18,185 --> 00:08:22,105
Understood. Please submit
a Uniform Exception form after class.

61
00:08:22,773 --> 00:08:24,316
Now let us begin today's lesson.

62
00:08:48,423 --> 00:08:52,678
I would like to ask all students
to log into the Green Room for meditation.

63
00:08:52,761 --> 00:08:54,346
Counting on ya, Doc…

64
00:08:59,184 --> 00:09:00,477
What's going on?

65
00:09:00,561 --> 00:09:01,520
It's Martinez.

66
00:09:01,603 --> 00:09:03,105
It's a virus!

67
00:09:09,111 --> 00:09:12,281
I'm so sorry
for the inconvenience he's caused.

68
00:09:12,364 --> 00:09:15,409
I wouldn't say this is just
a matter of money, Mrs. Martinez.

69
00:09:15,492 --> 00:09:19,371
Although it was
quite an expense to restore the system.

70
00:09:19,454 --> 00:09:22,207
Of course, and I will pay for the repairs.

71
00:09:22,291 --> 00:09:23,125
What?

72
00:09:23,208 --> 00:09:26,962
As I understand it,
David modified his headset

73
00:09:27,045 --> 00:09:30,632
with back-alley software
to avoid paying for the licensed update.

74
00:09:30,716 --> 00:09:34,595
With all due respect, could this be
related to some financial difficulties?

75
00:09:34,678 --> 00:09:37,889
It's no problem, really. We can afford it.

76
00:09:37,973 --> 00:09:41,852
I believe this is a good opportunity
to reconsider David's situation.

77
00:09:41,935 --> 00:09:43,145
What situation?

78
00:09:43,228 --> 00:09:47,524
Well, David doesn't fit in
with his classmates.

79
00:09:47,608 --> 00:09:49,568
A change in environment could benefit--

80
00:09:49,651 --> 00:09:52,571
No! He has to stay here.

81
00:09:52,654 --> 00:09:55,741
He deserves this education
as much as every other kid here…

82
00:09:56,366 --> 00:09:58,744
Didn't I tell you to get the upgrade?

83
00:09:59,328 --> 00:10:02,331
Doc's fault, he gave me a busted drive…

84
00:10:02,414 --> 00:10:07,419
You tried to outsmart the system and now
we owe ten times the original cost.

85
00:10:07,502 --> 00:10:09,004
Sorry…

86
00:10:09,087 --> 00:10:12,591
If you're gonna apologize anyway,
don't do it in the first place.

87
00:10:12,674 --> 00:10:15,469
You said you didn't have the eddies
first time I asked…

88
00:10:15,552 --> 00:10:18,013
Because it wasn't payday yet!

89
00:10:18,096 --> 00:10:20,474
Of course we don't got cash
just lying around!

90
00:10:20,557 --> 00:10:22,726
And can't you sit still?

91
00:10:25,187 --> 00:10:28,023
Y'know, I've been thinking lately…

92
00:10:28,106 --> 00:10:29,608
About?

93
00:10:29,691 --> 00:10:33,111
Maybe I drop out…
Find work now or whatever.

94
00:10:33,195 --> 00:10:34,738
Do you hear yourself?!

95
00:10:34,821 --> 00:10:38,909
C'mon, seriously.
You know we can't afford those repairs.

96
00:10:38,992 --> 00:10:43,497
Plus, you got no clue
how much I stick out.

97
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:46,917
Anyone who's not a true-blue corpo
gets shit on constantly.

98
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:51,672
They'll never accept me,
even if I do graduate.

99
00:10:52,255 --> 00:10:54,341
Don't wanna be a corpo anyway.

100
00:10:57,761 --> 00:11:00,722
Then what've I been busting my ass for?

101
00:11:02,015 --> 00:11:07,688
Everything I do is for you, Dee…
Don't you see that?

102
00:11:08,897 --> 00:11:11,024
You're breaking my heart.

103
00:11:11,108 --> 00:11:12,150
Mom…?

104
00:11:12,234 --> 00:11:16,780
My baby boy… So smart and so talented.

105
00:11:16,863 --> 00:11:21,618
I just wanna give you a fighting chance
in this city, a good education…

106
00:11:22,327 --> 00:11:27,124
That's why I put in the hours,
why I'm never home!

107
00:11:29,126 --> 00:11:31,086
I'm sorry.

108
00:11:31,169 --> 00:11:35,048
Shouldn't have brought it up.
Don't cry, mom…

109
00:11:35,132 --> 00:11:38,343
You think I don't know how they treat you?

110
00:11:38,427 --> 00:11:40,887
You think I don't get treated
the same way?

111
00:11:40,971 --> 00:11:43,598
But that's why you gotta prove 'em wrong.

112
00:11:43,682 --> 00:11:45,517
I want you to work hard, rise up,

113
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:49,896
and get to the top floor of Arasaka Tower!

114
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:52,607
I know you got it in you, Dee.

115
00:11:53,275 --> 00:11:55,485
Easier said than… done…

116
00:12:01,616 --> 00:12:03,118
Fuck 'em up!

117
00:12:05,287 --> 00:12:06,496
Don't let 'em get away!

118
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:08,665
Fuck! Suit's limo's plated!

119
00:12:08,748 --> 00:12:12,627
The hunt's on, beastbros!

120
00:12:23,054 --> 00:12:25,849
No one fucks with the Animals!

121
00:12:25,932 --> 00:12:27,684
Mom! Brake hard!

122
00:12:27,767 --> 00:12:28,810
Mom!

123
00:12:40,238 --> 00:12:41,323
Mom?

124
00:12:41,907 --> 00:12:43,116
Mom!

125
00:12:50,415 --> 00:12:53,418
Trauma Team? Thank God…

126
00:12:56,421 --> 00:12:58,215
Not a client.

127
00:12:58,298 --> 00:12:59,216
Neither is she.

128
00:12:59,299 --> 00:13:00,133
Wait!

129
00:13:00,217 --> 00:13:03,970
Secure the policy holder.
Leave these guys to the city meat wagons.

130
00:13:04,054 --> 00:13:05,722
-Copy that.
-What?!

131
00:13:05,805 --> 00:13:08,475
What the hell? Hey! Wait!

132
00:13:09,643 --> 00:13:10,727
Shit!

133
00:13:10,810 --> 00:13:12,729
You're just gonna leave us here?!

134
00:13:13,313 --> 00:13:15,732
Mom!

135
00:13:15,815 --> 00:13:17,734
Wake up!

136
00:13:17,817 --> 00:13:19,736
Fucking piece of…

137
00:13:19,819 --> 00:13:24,032
Mom! Damn it, get off me!

138
00:13:24,115 --> 00:13:27,994
Get the fuck off! Damn it!

139
00:13:28,078 --> 00:13:30,956
Shit, shit, shit!

140
00:13:31,039 --> 00:13:32,749
Shit!

141
00:13:36,294 --> 00:13:41,216
Surgery was a success. She hasn't come to
just yet, but she's stable.

142
00:13:41,299 --> 00:13:43,426
We'll keep her
a few more nights to observe.

143
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:45,637
Oh… Can't I see her?

144
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:49,516
No can do, kid.
Visitation's not part of your package.

145
00:13:49,599 --> 00:13:51,184
R-Right…

146
00:13:51,268 --> 00:13:56,147
Anyway, here's some paperwork and
your bill. Brought your mom's things, too.

147
00:13:56,231 --> 00:13:58,316
Zip us those eddies within three days.

148
00:13:58,400 --> 00:13:59,234
Uh…

149
00:13:59,818 --> 00:14:03,113
There's a reason everyone
in Night City wants insurance, kid.

150
00:14:03,196 --> 00:14:04,239
Have a good one.

151
00:14:05,198 --> 00:14:07,492
Yeah, yeah, looking for
a buyer for a hoops chip…

152
00:14:08,368 --> 00:14:11,496
You gotta be low-balling me,
That's all? What?

153
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:14,416
Nah, forget it, choom.

154
00:14:14,499 --> 00:14:15,792
Damn it!

155
00:14:18,962 --> 00:14:20,630
What the fuck?!

156
00:14:28,138 --> 00:14:30,557
There's another account…

157
00:14:31,141 --> 00:14:33,101
Never knew she saved so much…

158
00:14:33,643 --> 00:14:36,563
So, this settles the medical…

159
00:14:38,773 --> 00:14:40,901
Gotta cover the rent.

160
00:14:42,152 --> 00:14:45,363
Doc? Hey, you get the still I sent?

161
00:14:45,447 --> 00:14:50,702
Listen, don't think I've forgotten about
that shoddy bootleg you gave me…

162
00:14:50,785 --> 00:14:51,995
Ugh. Whatever, man.

163
00:14:52,704 --> 00:14:57,834
This cyberware…
Yeah, looks military-grade, right?

164
00:14:57,918 --> 00:15:02,422
What do you think it could fetch?

165
00:15:03,089 --> 00:15:05,258
Not selling. Just want an estimate.

166
00:15:07,886 --> 00:15:11,097
Nah, fuck that noise,
no way it's that cheap.

167
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:15,977
C'mon, choom.

168
00:15:18,104 --> 00:15:20,023
Whatever, wasn't selling anyway.

169
00:15:20,106 --> 00:15:23,944
And don't expect me to push
your XBDs at school anymore!

170
00:15:26,196 --> 00:15:27,948
Taking me for a gonk…

171
00:15:29,741 --> 00:15:31,618
A Sandevistan…

172
00:15:31,701 --> 00:15:36,122
No serial.
Military-grade, this thing, really?

173
00:15:36,206 --> 00:15:39,084
Definitely ain't legal, but…

174
00:15:39,167 --> 00:15:42,253
Whoa! The hell are these specs?!

175
00:16:01,773 --> 00:16:06,361
Drop out of the Academy.
Learn to take a hint, David Martinez.

176
00:16:06,444 --> 00:16:07,404
About what?

177
00:16:07,487 --> 00:16:10,281
Our class. You're not welcome.

178
00:16:10,365 --> 00:16:11,825
If this is about yesterday--

179
00:16:11,908 --> 00:16:14,244
Who said anything about yesterday?

180
00:16:14,327 --> 00:16:17,789
You think I give you a hard time
'cause you're poor? No.

181
00:16:17,872 --> 00:16:19,916
In fact, I consider myself charitable.

182
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,502
And it's not your fault
that you were born poor.

183
00:16:23,086 --> 00:16:26,214
There's no rule that says
a street kid can't attend the Academy,

184
00:16:26,297 --> 00:16:28,633
provided they pay tuition, of course.

185
00:16:28,717 --> 00:16:31,469
What cracks my chrome is
something else entirely.

186
00:16:31,553 --> 00:16:32,762
-Know what it is?
-Choom…

187
00:16:32,846 --> 00:16:35,181
I haven't understood
a thing outta your mouth.

188
00:16:35,265 --> 00:16:36,725
That right there!

189
00:16:36,808 --> 00:16:39,477
Drop out. Get gone.

190
00:16:39,561 --> 00:16:40,395
What?

191
00:16:40,478 --> 00:16:42,230
You're a misfit, an anomaly.

192
00:16:42,313 --> 00:16:48,361
Human trash. And nothing can change that.
Rot goes as deep as your bones.

193
00:16:48,445 --> 00:16:51,865
Best you can do
is not spread it to the rest of us.

194
00:16:51,948 --> 00:16:53,491
Did I short-circ?

195
00:16:53,575 --> 00:16:56,202
Thought you didn't care
so long as I paid tuition.

196
00:16:56,286 --> 00:17:01,249
I heard mommy came to see the principal
to beg for forgiveness yesterday.

197
00:17:01,332 --> 00:17:05,503
Caused quite a scene, crying for
her baby boy not to get expelled, right?

198
00:17:05,587 --> 00:17:06,880
Shameless.

199
00:17:06,963 --> 00:17:09,591
Y'know, it's always been a mystery to me…

200
00:17:09,674 --> 00:17:13,136
How could she afford to send you
to Arasaka Academy in the first place?

201
00:17:13,219 --> 00:17:16,139
Care to explain, David Martinez?

202
00:17:16,222 --> 00:17:20,643
What does mommy do
to pay your way through school?

203
00:17:20,727 --> 00:17:26,316
What does any Night City bottom-feeder do
to make a quick eurobuck, huh?

204
00:17:26,399 --> 00:17:28,443
A couple of things come to mind…

205
00:17:28,526 --> 00:17:29,652
Enough of this shit.

206
00:17:29,736 --> 00:17:31,905
Whoa, who said we were done?

207
00:17:31,988 --> 00:17:33,239
Fuck off!

208
00:17:35,533 --> 00:17:36,409
The hell?

209
00:17:43,166 --> 00:17:45,126
Huh? What?

210
00:17:45,210 --> 00:17:46,628
Oh?

211
00:17:46,711 --> 00:17:48,630
Huuuh?

212
00:17:53,093 --> 00:17:56,513
What's that you've got slotted?
Some kind of freeware?

213
00:18:22,497 --> 00:18:28,044
The Strongarms 400 really does
bring out the best in kung-fu chipware.

214
00:18:28,128 --> 00:18:30,088
Seriously? Organic knuckles?

215
00:18:30,171 --> 00:18:34,134
If you wanna try me again,
better pack some chrome.

216
00:18:34,634 --> 00:18:37,011
Or just drop out of school already.

217
00:18:44,519 --> 00:18:51,192
Mr. Martinez? I'm calling in regard to
Gloria Martinez's condition…

218
00:18:52,485 --> 00:18:57,699
She was stable this morning,
but her vitals nosedived out of nowhere.

219
00:18:58,283 --> 00:19:02,662
But you said…
You said the surgery went fine.

220
00:19:02,745 --> 00:19:04,914
Her body was already weak.

221
00:19:04,998 --> 00:19:08,585
She wouldn't have lasted long even if
she wasn't on the discount package.

222
00:19:08,668 --> 00:19:10,670
Looked like she was overworked.

223
00:19:11,212 --> 00:19:14,465
Here are some burial options we offer.

224
00:19:14,549 --> 00:19:18,386
There's a reason everyone wants
a corporate gig in Night City, kid.

225
00:19:18,469 --> 00:19:21,347
Valued customer,
we are sorry for your loss.

226
00:19:21,431 --> 00:19:25,852
We can deliver the body of the deceased
to your home or funeral center.

227
00:19:25,935 --> 00:19:29,480
Would you like to hear
about our payment plans?

228
00:19:30,064 --> 00:19:31,816
Do I have a choice?

229
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:35,737
Is our budget-friendly
cremation service right for you?

230
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:37,947
Waive those pesky delivery fees and…

231
00:19:46,039 --> 00:19:47,248
Good day, Mrs. Martinez.

232
00:19:47,332 --> 00:19:51,461
We've received a quote for the repairs
to our damaged system infrastructure.

233
00:19:51,544 --> 00:19:56,966
I've sent you the details as agreed.
Or perhaps you've had time to reflect?

234
00:19:57,050 --> 00:20:02,222
If you can't make the payment on time,
we'll have no choice but to expel David…

235
00:20:02,305 --> 00:20:05,725
If you wish to continue
your utilities contract,

236
00:20:05,808 --> 00:20:09,062
you will need to pay
a penalty of 500 eurodollars

237
00:20:09,145 --> 00:20:13,524
in addition to any past due
amounts and late fees.

238
00:20:13,608 --> 00:20:17,946
If you are unable to make the payment,
your utilities will be shut down…

239
00:20:18,029 --> 00:20:20,698
Trauma Team. Clear the way immediately.

240
00:20:21,407 --> 00:20:26,496
Ding ding, Martinez! Time's up!
Rent's long overdue!

241
00:20:26,579 --> 00:20:29,415
Keep this shit up
and I won't just be changing your lock.

242
00:20:29,499 --> 00:20:34,379
I'll throw your ass out
on the street, hear me?!

243
00:20:49,811 --> 00:20:53,606
The implant I showed you…
You said you'd take it for 10K?

244
00:20:54,274 --> 00:20:58,278
Six now? Choom, no.
Just yesterday you said 10!

245
00:20:58,361 --> 00:21:00,655
You and I both know it's worth way more!

246
00:21:00,738 --> 00:21:02,824
Yeah, I looked into it, and…

247
00:21:05,576 --> 00:21:08,204
Oh yeah? Fine! Fuck you too!

248
00:21:08,288 --> 00:21:09,330
Fuck!

249
00:22:00,590 --> 00:22:02,633
The hell… Who is it?

250
00:22:03,259 --> 00:22:05,470
Oh. David, hey.

251
00:22:06,471 --> 00:22:07,680
That the big, bad Sandy?

252
00:22:07,764 --> 00:22:14,145
There's not a badge or fixer in town
who's not looking for that beauty.

253
00:22:14,228 --> 00:22:18,191
I told ya, you ain't gonna find anyone
sane enough to take it off your hands.

254
00:22:18,274 --> 00:22:19,817
I'm not here to sell.

